{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-run-server-panel-worker-b-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"gap-8","surface":"server","area":"server/panel-worker","refs":["F-server-125"],"severity":"S3","title":"Connecting a payment company by signing in can fail with no log line saying why","what":"When an owner uses the sign-in Connect button for Razorpay or Cashfree and the company refuses to start the sign-in or to hand over the keys afterwards, the owner is sent back to the Payments page with a short refused line. The server writes nothing: not the company's answer, not its status. MettleUp cannot tell a wrong client setting from a company outage when an owner says connecting does not work. The feature is behind a switch today.","expected":"Each refused start or key hand-over writes one log line with the company, the test or live mode and the company's status, with no keys in it.","evidence":["deploy/panel/pay.js:1617-1623","deploy/panel/pay.js:1638-1642","deploy/panel/pay.js:1673-1674","deploy/panel/pay.js:1685-1686"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"oauth-refusal-not-logged","who":"owners and HQ","how_often":"only when the company refuses the sign-in","fix_line":"Log the company's status on both refused paths before sending the owner back","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
